Subject: [PATCH 4/8] scene: A chain of menus stacks one popped limit per level

A chain of popups shared the popped limit among its members, so opening a
sub-menu moved its parent back (menu 5 alone, then 3 with a sub-menu at 5, at a
limit of 5). Level n now sits n popped limits from its base, whatever the length
of the chain: the screen for a plain window, the pinned window's level for a
window kept above the others (Daniel, 2026-11-08: "two menu levels will yeld
twice the separation from the screen, three levels the same"). A menu opened
alone stays at the limit, opening a sub-menu moves nothing above it, each level
is drawn above its parent, a dialog is a level of the chain (a combo box's
list or a menu opened in it is the level beyond it), and the chain stops
growing at six levels. A popup
with no parent (an X11 override-redirect menu) is the n-th such popup in the
stacking order. Notifications and on-screen displays are as ORDERs 424 and 442
built them; the edge rule and the larger-than-the-room exception stay.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
